  "subtitle": "Main example: valid KOL A session → later valid KOL B click in the same Shop → checkout.",
  "classNote": "Unique AttributionSession(storeId, visitorIdHash) stores the winning KOL/link. Cookie contains signed visitor identity; Order session/click IDs are scalars, not invented foreign keys.",
  "notes": [
    "Precondition: a prior valid A click created the visitor session; the diagram expands the later B click. Different Stores keep separate sessions. Window defaults to 30 days, configurable per Store from 1 to 365.",
    "Browser = RedirectHandlerPage + checkout UI. Traffic limiter, link cache, independent click worker and fingerprint fallback internals are summarized in FR13_CODE_ANALYSIS.md. Ineligible clicks do not replace the session.",
    "Checkout reads and writes occur within the same order transaction; the separate read/write arrows summarize its callback. Active, unexpired session/link/KOL checks apply. Cookie is not a trusted KOL ID supplied by the client."
  ],
